| `scripts/git_tree.py` | The one definition of what git lists: a snapshot and a digest of the work tree, whether a path is ignored, which given paths git tracks (`tracked`), HEAD's commit, the files a commit could carry (`candidate_files`), the files the next commit adds or changes (`staged_paths`, which reads the index a hook's `GIT_INDEX_FILE` names when asked for git's repository context) and a file's index copy (`staged_blob`). It raises `NoGitError` only when git is not installed or there is no repository, and `GitFailedError` for every other git failure. confined_path checks resolved paths without git and raises PathEscape for escapes, symlink loops or unreadable ancestors, while allowing internal links and missing targets. | imported | — | Git listings exclude ignored paths; confined_path judges paths independently of git. Stays stdlib-only and 3.6-safe. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
